<title>BELGIUM: France opposes proposal to cut EU cereals aid.</title>
<headline>France opposes proposal to cut EU cereals aid.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's new farm minister Louis Le Pensec rejected a proposal to cut aid payments to cereals and oilseed farmers, a European Commission spokesman said on Friday.</p>
<p>But the French minister added during a first meeting with EU Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler that a reduction could be discussed in the context of future farm reforms, the spokesman said,</p>
<p>Fischler has called for a 1.4 billion ecus cut in cereals and oilseeds compensatory payments to help finance aid for beef producers hit by the mad cow crisis.</p>
<p>The proposal, which is opposed by all EU countries except Britain and Sweden, is attached to the 1997/98 (July/June) farm price package which is due to be agreed by EU farm ministers in Luxembourg next week.</p>
<p>-Brussels newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
